# Day 49

## Experiment Title

Building Applications using Jenkins


## Objective

To understand how Jenkins is used to automate application build processes.


## Theory

Jenkins allows developers to automate software builds through jobs and pipelines. Automated builds help ensure that application code is compiled and verified regularly without manual intervention.

Jenkins can integrate with source code repositories and automatically trigger builds whenever changes are pushed to the project. Build automation improves software quality and development efficiency.


## Requirements

Jenkins

Java Development Kit

GitHub Repository

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the Jenkins dashboard.

Create or open an existing Jenkins project.

Configure source code repository settings.

Add build steps for application compilation.

Save the project configuration.

Execute the build process and monitor build activity.


## Output

The application build process executed successfully in Jenkins.

Build details and execution logs were displayed correctly.

The application was compiled successfully through Jenkins automation.


## Result

Successfully automated the application build process using Jenkins.
